"The Escherichia coli protein YjjG is a house-cleaning nucleotidase in vivo - PubMed (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17286574/)\nciteturn242search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # The Escherichia coli protein YjjG is a house-cleaning nucleotidase in vivo ...   * PMID: 17286574 ...   * Search in PubMed\n\n. 2007 May;270(1):49-57.\n\ndoi: 10.1111/j.1574-6968.2007.00646.x. Epub 2007 Feb 5.\n\n# The Escherichia coli protein YjjG is a house-cleaning nucleotidase in vivo\n\nBjörn Titz^{  1 }, Roman Häuser, Anne Engelbrecher, Peter Uetz\n\nAffiliations Expand\n\n### Affiliation\n\n  * ^{1} Institute of Genetics, Forschungszentrum Karlsruhe, Karlsruhe, Germany. bjoern@itg.fzk.de\n\n  * PMID: 17286574\n  * DOI: 10.1111/j.1574-6968.2007.00646.x\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# The Escherichia coli protein YjjG is a house-cleaning nucleotidase in vivo\n\nBjörn Titz et al. FEMS Microbiol Lett. 2007 May.\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat [Select]\n\n[Button: FEMS Microbiol Lett ]\n\nActions\n\n  * Search in PubMed\n  * Search in NLM Catalog\n  * Add to Search\n\n. 2007 May;270(1):49-57.\n\ndoi: 10.1111/j.1574-6968.2007.00646.x. Epub 2007 Feb 5.\n\n### Authors\n\nBjörn Titz^{  1 }, Roman Häuser, Anne Engelbrecher, Peter Uetz\n\n### Affiliation\n\n  * ^{1} Institute of Genetics, Forschungszentrum Karlsruhe, Karlsruhe, Germany. bjoern@itg.fzk.de\n\n  * PMID: 17286574\n  * DOI: 10.1111/j.1574-6968.2007.00646.x\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n[Button: Full text links ]Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat [Select]\n\n## Abstract\n\nHouse-cleaning enzymes protect cells from the adverse effects of noncanonical metabolic chemical compounds. The Escherichia coli nucleotide phosphatase YjjG (B4374, JW4336) functions as a house-cleaning phosphatase in vivo. YjjG protects the cell against noncanonical pyrimidine derivatives such as 5-fluoro-2'-deoxyuridine (5-FdUridine), 5-fluorouridine, 5-fluoroorotic acid (5-FOA), 5-fluorouracil, and 5-aza-2'-deoxycytidine. YjjG prevents the incorporation of potentially mutagenic nucleotides into DNA as shown for 5-bromo-2'-deoxyuridine (BrdU). Its enzymatic activity in vitro towards noncanonical 5-fluoro-2'-deoxyuridine monophosphate (5-FdUMP) is higher than towards canonical thymidine monophosphate (dTMP). The closest homolog in humans, HDHD4, does not show a protective effect against noncanonical nucleotides, excluding an involvement of HDHD4 in resistance against noncanonical nucleotides used for cancer chemotherapy. The substrate spectrum of YjjG suggests that its in vivo substrates are noncanonical pyrimidine derivatives, which might also include oxidized nucleobases such as 5-formyluracil and 5-hydroxyuracil.\n\n\n## Publication types\n\n  * [Button: Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n## MeSH terms\n\n  * [Button: Azacitidine / analogs & derivatives ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Azacitidine / chemistry ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Azacitidine / pharmacology ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Bromodeoxyuridine / pharmacology ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: DNA Damage ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Decitabine ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Deoxyuridine / chemistry ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Deoxyuridine / pharmacology ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\n  * [Button: Escherichia coli / drug effects ]\n\nActions\n\n    * Search in PubMed\n    * Search in MeSH\n    * Add to Search\n\